# ---- Required: one model key and a Minecraft server ------------------------

# Jev through TypeSafe. Get a key at https://typesafe.ai/
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# The Minecraft Java 26.1 server the bot joins, and the name it plays as.
MC_HOST=localhost
MC_PORT=25565
MC_USERNAME=Jev
# "offline" for a LAN/offline-mode server, "microsoft" for a real account.
MC_AUTH=offline

# ---- Optional: generative model for custom building designs and stuck recovery

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_BUILD_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5
# auto uses the configured OpenRouter or guide model for Survival and Creative.
# guide uses JEV_GUIDE_API_KEY and JEV_GUIDE_URL. openrouter uses OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
# jev uses built-in houses and templates. JEV_BUILD_MODEL overrides the planner model.
# JEV_BUILD_MODEL=gpt-6.1-terra
BUILD_DESIGNER=auto
# jev: Jev picks a code-checked recovery action after repeated failures.
# off: ordinary retries only.
RECOVERY_ADVISER=jev

# ---- Optional: everything else ---------------------------------------------

# Jev decisions can also go through OpenRouter instead of TypeSafe.
# JEV_PROVIDER=typesafe
# JEV_PROVIDER=openrouter
# OPENROUTER_JEV_MODEL=typesafe/jev-1.14   (the runs use 1.14; 1.13, the code default, died about three times as often)
# TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL=jev-latest

# Pin the protocol version if auto-detection picks the wrong one.
# MC_VERSION=26.1
# A separate memory namespace when you replace the world at the same address.
# MC_WORLD_ID=my-survival-world

# What the bot does between requests. Unset: it looks after itself (food,
# shelter, supplies). wait: it stays where it stands and only answers what
# would hurt it there (lava, fire, drowning, a mob in reach). Waiting, it has
# two moves of its own, made by rule:
#   - back to its player after monsters: having given ground to a mob while a
#     player was within 32 blocks, it walks back to that player once it has
#     given none for three seconds and no monster is within 8 blocks of them
#     (company.js backDue). A bot told to stop walks back too, and stays
#     stopped; "stop" said during the walk ends it. Not a rule to follow: a
#     player who walks off afterwards is not gone after.
#   - to bed when the players go: with every other player in the game seen in
#     a bed, it lies down in a free bed standing within 16 blocks, and gets up
#     when one of them does (bedtime.js). It digs and places nothing for that;
#     with no free bed it says so once a night and stays up. A bot following a
#     player does the same. At night this needs JEV_NIGHT=company below, or
#     the bot is in its shelter by then.
# JEV_IDLE=wait

# ask: work one player gave is not replaced by another player's request until
# the first player says yes. Stop is never gated. Unset: any request replaces
# the work in hand.
# JEV_COOPERATION=ask

# What someone built is left alone: a village's houses, a player's base, a
# mine's timbers. Read from the blocks: planks, stairs, glass, a bed, a chest,
# and the logs and stone set among them. What the bot laid itself is its own.
#   leave   not taken, unless a player says it may ("Jev use the buildings"
#           for the work in hand; with the language layer also in plain words
#           with the request, "get 8 oak logs, you can take them from the
#           houses"), or the search for a free source has gone ten minutes
#           with none of it gained, which the bot says in chat as it gives in.
#   strict  only the player's word.
# Unset: the nearest source is taken, built or not. Not covered: village
# chests and ripe village crops (looting.js, villages.js), the Nether and End.
# JEV_BUILT=leave

# The night with a player. Unset: from dusk to dawn the bot takes shelter (a
# pocket dug where it stands, as a rule), whoever is about, and work on the
# surface waits for the morning.
#   company  while a player is within 32 blocks, and for 20 seconds after, it
#            stays up: it waits or works on as by day. A pocket sealed only
#            for the night is opened when a player comes within 16 blocks and
#            no mob is that near. Alone, it shelters as before. Mobs are
#            answered as ever (it runs or fights), so it dies more often,
#            above all before it has a weapon.
# JEV_NIGHT=company

# A sword kept about it (asked for 2026-11-23, src/keep-armed.js).
#   pockets  at work on a request with no stone sword or better carried, a
#            sword its pockets make with crafts alone is made before the next
#            step (iron, copper or stone; wooden only with no weapon at all),
#            never from the request's own item. A failed try rests ten minutes.
#   keep     that, and with JEV_IDLE=wait a waiting bot with no stone sword
#            or better goes and makes one, gathering for it by day (by night
#            only from what it carries), then walks back to the player it
#            waited with. "Stop" or any request ends it, nobody is asked
#            before a request replaces it, and an errand that failed, ran
#            eight minutes or left it with no sword rests ten minutes.
# JEV_WEAPON=pockets

# player: ore is found where the bot can see it, a face turned to it within
# 32 blocks with nothing solid in the way, and remembered once seen, not read
# through the rock from the loaded chunks. Underground it finds ore as a
# player does, in caves and in the walls of what it digs, and so more slowly.
# Unset: every vein in the loaded chunks within the search's reach.
# JEV_PERCEPTION=player

# The bot's own lines about what it is doing, each new step and what survival
# does (narration.js). off: none of them, answers to players only. important:
# only survival's (a run, a meal, a shelter). Unset or full: all of them.
# JEV_NARRATION=important

# A language model in front of the request interpreter, for guidance in plain
# words: standing rules ("from now on, wood means birch"), vague or two-step
# wishes, questions. It only produces chat lines and plain requests; it cannot
# run commands. Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint. Off when the
# key is empty. Each chat message addressed to the bot is one small model call
# (about 950 tokens in, 45 out).
# JEV_GUIDE_API_KEY=
# JEV_GUIDE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
# Measured on 31 scripted cases (scripts/guide-eval.js, scripts/guide-eval-hard.js), five runs
# each (2026-11-20), on the instructions as they are now:
#   gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning low   155 of 155, median 1.3 s   (the default)
#   gpt-6-luna, reasoning none     154 of 155, median 1.0 s   (about a tenth of the price)
# gpt-4.1-mini scored 45 of 51 on an earlier, shorter set.
# With JEV_BUILT set the instructions gain the rule about buildings and the wood
# standing free near the bot (about 1,270 tokens in, 51 out a call). On the 31 cases
# and the 12 of scripts/guide-eval-built.js, five runs each (2026-11-21):
#   gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning low   215 of 215, median 1.3 to 1.5 s
# JEV_GUIDE_MODEL=gpt-6.1-terra
# none, low, medium or high; empty sends none at all. A model that refuses the
# setting, or a temperature, is called again without it.
# JEV_GUIDE_REASONING=low
# JEV_GUIDE_TEMPERATURE=
# JEV_GUIDE_MAX_TOKENS=600
# JEV_GUIDE_PER_HOUR=60
# How the layer's chat lines sound: reserved (brief and calm), companion
# (curious and conversational) or playful (a light joke now and then). It
# changes the wording only, never what is asked of the engine. Unset: as
# measured above. Replies are in the language the player wrote in either way.
# JEV_PERSONALITY=companion

# Players allowed to ask for server commands ("Jev make it daytime").
# Empty disables them. The bot also needs operator permission on the server.
MC_COMMAND_USERS=

# The bot records what it sees and decides to .bot-state/flight (kept a day)
# for the audits; set to 0 to turn that off.
# JEV_FLIGHT=1

# Development drills (scripts/arena.js, terrain.js, endgame.js): a player the
# drill puts in Spectator on the bot so a run can be watched. Leave empty to
# watch nothing.
# ARENA_WATCHER=YourPlayerName

# Trials: the player made an operator on every trial server, to spectate Jev.
# TRIAL_WATCHER=YourPlayerName
# Where ReplayMod recordings go for the death montage (default: a macOS PrismLauncher instance).
# REPLAY_RECORDINGS=/path/to/replay_recordings
